[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438188455","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98524#issuecomment-2438188455","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98524","id":2438188455,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RU82n","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T15:54:00Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T15:54:00Z","body":"What is the expected behavior? How will your new behavior treat lost data like missing node or missing resource?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438188455/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438274907","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98524#issuecomment-2438274907","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98524","id":2438274907,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RVR9b","user":{"login":"Hex4F","id":75822970,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1ODIyOTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75822970?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F","html_url":"https://github.com/Hex4F","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T16:32:19Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T16:32:19Z","body":"@fire The obvious behavior would be to throw a warning or error when a resource/scene tries to set an exported property that isn't there. Even failing silently, discarding the override, would be fine. But it shouldn't quietly override the variable, and it certainly shouldn't be impossible to view or edit the override from the inspector.\r\n\r\nAm I not making the bug clear? I'm not talking about changing a property in GDScript. I'm talking about changing the value in the inspector, removing `@export` from the script, and now the value set in the inspector remains forever--even though you can't see it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438274907/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438313494","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98524#issuecomment-2438313494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98524","id":2438313494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RVbYW","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T16:50:06Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T16:50:06Z","body":"A key feature the other members of the Godot Engine team wanted was to not store the default values in the resource or packed scene.\r\n\r\nSo I don't know how to have both. We've also vetoed storing the default values per version forever in a database.\r\n\r\n> impossible to view or edit the override from the inspector\r\n\r\nThis is a separate bug.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438313494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438388437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98524#issuecomment-2438388437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98524","id":2438388437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RVtrV","user":{"login":"Hex4F","id":75822970,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1ODIyOTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75822970?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F","html_url":"https://github.com/Hex4F","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T17:18:37Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T17:18:46Z","body":"> This is a separate bug.\r\n\r\nWhat are you talking about? That _is_ the bug. The inspector shouldn't override variables that aren't marked `@export`, or it should be raising hell in the logs for trying.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438388437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438448370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98524#issuecomment-2438448370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98524","id":2438448370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RV8Ty","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T17:54:27Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T17:54:27Z","body":"Sometimes the editor makes fake inspector properties or doubles","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438448370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438586441","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98524#issuecomment-2438586441","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98524","id":2438586441,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RWeBJ","user":{"login":"Hex4F","id":75822970,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1ODIyOTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75822970?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F","html_url":"https://github.com/Hex4F","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hex4F/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T18:50:16Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T18:50:16Z","body":"I've never had that happen. My issue is with resource loading and probably trivially solved by Godot checking if a property is `@export` before letting the resource overwrite it. Not the _script_, which can access all properties by design, but the TSCN file format (and friends) that specify values for exported properties. These resource formats can specify values for any other _non-exported_ property as well, even though you can't view or edit them, and that strange behavior is almost certainly unintended. If Godot was designed to have these invisible properties, it wouldn't discard them when you save the file again.\r\n\r\nMaybe I caused confusion by bringing up the inspector because it's what you use to edit TSCN files. The inspector doesn't even need to be involved other than if this weird behavior has to stay, the inspector should say _something_ about these ghost properties that don't have `@export`.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2438586441/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]